    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present to the market 2 Mask Drive, Artane, Dublin 5, a well-positioned two-bedroom end of terrace property which offers excellent potential for\nthose seeking a comfortable home with versatile additional accommodation.\n\nThis appealing property benefits from an attic conversion together with a granny flat to the rear, providing a range of options for modern family living, working from home, guest accommodation or those looking for additional living space.\n\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully arranged over the main and upper levels and briefly comprises an entrance porch, entrance hallway, living room, kitchen/dining\narea, utility room, landing, two bedrooms, bathroom and attic room.\n\nOn entering the property, the entrance porch leads into a welcoming hallway which provides access to the principal living accommodation. The living room offers a\ncomfortable reception space and provides a natural focal point for the home. To the rear, the kitchen/dining area provides a practical and versatile space for everyday\nfamily life.\n\nUpstairs, the landing leads to two well proportioned bedrooms and the main family bathroom. The converted attic room provides valuable additional space and further enhances the versatility of the property.\nA particularly attractive feature of this home is the granny flat to the rear, offering excellent flexibility and potential for a variety of uses. This additional accommodation could prove particularly useful for extended family, guests, a home office or hobby space.\n\nThere is off street car parking to the front of the property while side access leads to a private south facing rear garden.\n\nSituated in Artane, Dublin 5, the property enjoys the convenience of a well-established residential location, with a host of local amenities and services available nearby. The area is well served by public transport and provides easy access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding suburbs.\n\nViewing comes highly recommended."
      },
